  "note": "Urban district election, 15 January 1923; whole council elected at large. Polling on Monday 15 January; twelve vacancies and thirteen candidates. Register 1,231, of whom 913 voted; five spoiled papers. The defeated candidate is named in the report as Mr. William Murray."
